{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"callous-quenched-blackrhino","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\nParity gap found while fixing bug 2be7 (whitespace-only description edits invalidating a\nsigned plan review). 2be7 canonicalizes insignificant whitespace out of the **description**\nbefore it enters the material basis. The basis has a second free-text field that is still\nhashed raw.\n\n`material_basis()` in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py` adds, when the ticket\ndeclares no file impact:\n\n    basis[\"file_impact_scope\"] = {\n        \"kind\": \"none\",\n        \"reason\": reason if isinstance(reason, str) else \"\",\n    }\n\n`reason` is operator-supplied free text and goes into the hash verbatim. A trailing space or\na line-ending difference in it moves the composite fingerprint and stales a signed\nattestation, exactly as a trailing newline in the description used to.\n\n## Why it was left out of 2be7\n\nDeliberate scope control, not an oversight:\n\n- 2be7's proven root cause and its reproduction are both about the **description** — the\n  concrete repro is `rebar edit --description=\"$(cat file)\"`, where shell command\n  substitution strips a trailing newline from a long multi-line document. `reason` is a short\n  single-line string that is not normally round-tripped through a file, so it does not have\n  that failure mode.\n- The material fingerprint is a security control: it exists so an attestation cannot survive\n  a substantive plan change. Every widening of the canonicalized surface must arrive with its\n  own RED test proving that meaningful edits to that field still invalidate. Bolting a second\n  field onto 2be7 without that proof is precisely the over-widening 2be7 was careful to avoid.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nApply the existing `normalize_insignificant_whitespace()` (added by 2be7, same module) to\n`reason` at the same single point in `material_basis`. Mirror 2be7's test shape: a\nwhitespace-only edit to the reason keeps the fingerprint and reads `certified`; a\nmeaningful edit to it still reads `stale-material`.\n\nNote the legacy generations in `attest._legacy_material_ok` — the pre-330c (raw) and\npost-330c/pre-2be7 (checkbox-only) recomputes — would need the same treatment as 2be7 gave\nthem if pre-existing attestations over a declared-none ticket are to be grandfathered.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A whitespace-only edit to `no_file_impact_reason` does not change the material\n      fingerprint, so a signed plan review stays `certified` per `rebar review-plan --status`.\n- [ ] A semantically meaningful edit to `no_file_impact_reason` still invalidates the\n      attestation (`stale-material`), proven by a negative-control test.\n- [ ] The pre-330c legacy path still hashes the raw reason, so bug 96d1's grandfather is\n      not regressed (`tests/unit/test_legacy_material_grandfather_96d1.py` passes untouched).","id":"8aed-f307-8faa-49c6","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"no_file_impact_reason is hashed raw into plan-review material, so whitespace-only edits to it still stale an attestation"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786106983674723001,"uuid":"38d7abc8-93b3-4cfb-9e8d-543010fe3dd4"}